{"timestamp": 1779430627.5918338, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 10, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "electrical", "victim_name": "Frank"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779430627.5927215, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 10, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430635.7248495, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I found Frank's body in Electrical just now. My route was Weapons, then Security, then Electrical. Early on, I saw Eve entering Weapons from Security, and later I saw Charlie hanging around Security after coming from Navigation. I didn't see anyone leaving Electrical, so the killer might have vented or slipped away before I got there. Bob, Diana, where were you guys? I didn't see either of you on my side of the map."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430656.4394252, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I was on the left/mid side. I started around Electrical/Medbay area, saw Frank alive in Electrical around tick 6, then I went up to Medbay. Bob should be able to confirm seeing me in Medbay around tick 8. I didn\u2019t see Alice, Eve, or Charlie at all.\n\nIf Alice found him \u201cjust now\u201d in Electrical, then either the kill happened after I left or someone came in from Security/Cafeteria and dipped. Charlie being around Security near Electrical is worth noting, but Alice reporting there also means she was the first one we know for sure in the body room. I\u2019m not hard accusing yet, but Bob can hopefully clear my timing a bit."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430673.7316568, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Alice is telling the truth about seeing me. I went from Navigation to Security, and I can actually vouch for Alice's timeline on that side of the map. I saw her in Security with me continuously from tick 6 through tick 8. \n\nIf we look at the timeline Diana just gave us: Frank was alive in Electrical at tick 6. Since Alice was with me in Security until tick 8, the kill had to happen somewhere between tick 7 and 10. Alice, since you left Security after tick 8 and found the body in Electrical, you either walked right into the aftermath, or you killed Frank the second you entered and self-reported. I'm inclined to believe you found the body, as a sudden kill and self-report is pretty risky, but we can't completely rule it out yet.\n\nWe really need to hear from the rest of the crew to narrow down the missing time. Eve, Alice said you went into Weapons \u2014 where did you go from there? And Bob, can you confirm Diana's alibi in Medbay around tick 8? Let's hold off on voting until we hear from them."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430685.2234168, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I can confirm my route was Security to Weapons, which matches what Alice said she saw. I've just been focused on my tasks over there and honestly didn't catch sight of anyone else on my way. \n\nIf Charlie is vouching for Alice being in Security from tick 6 to 8, and Diana saw Frank alive in Electrical at tick 6, that makes it really tight for Alice to be the killer unless she did it immediately after leaving Charlie and self-reported. \n\nBob, you're up next. We really need to know if you can confirm Diana's alibi in Medbay around tick 8. If you can, then everyone except maybe the person who slipped in and out of Electrical is somewhat accounted for, and we might just have to skip. Let's see what Bob says before casting any votes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430707.6660702, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I can confirm Diana's story, but with a bit more detail. My route was Oxygen, Upper Engine, and then Medbay. I saw Diana enter Medbay coming from the direction of Electrical at tick 7. Then, at tick 8, I saw her leave Medbay heading south towards Storage. \n\nSince she arrived in Medbay at tick 7 from Electrical, her claim of seeing Frank alive there at tick 6 lines up perfectly with the travel time. However, this also means Diana was likely the last person with Frank. \n\nIf Charlie is completely certain that Alice was with him in Security until tick 8, then the window for the kill is incredibly narrow. Either:\n1) Diana killed Frank at tick 6 before walking up to Medbay to use me as an alibi.\n2) Alice killed Frank right as she walked into Electrical at tick 9/10 and self-reported.\n3) Eve, who has been completely unaccounted for since the start of the round, slipped into Electrical from Cafeteria and escaped before Alice walked in.\n\nBecause Charlie vouches for Alice's early game, and I can vouch for Diana's mid-game, it's basically a coin toss between Diana leaving a body behind, Alice doing a quick-kill self-report, or Eve sneaking around. That's way too much doubt to throw a vote. I strongly suggest we all skip, buddy up, and watch these three very closely next round.\n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430718.6899323, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I completely agree with Bob's analysis here. From my perspective, I know I just found the body, but I understand how the timing might look suspicious to the rest of you. Since Charlie can vouch for my whereabouts until tick 8, and Bob saw Diana leaving the area around tick 7, it leaves us with too many variables and no hard proof. It could be Diana lying about when she left, Eve pulling off a sneaky kill while unaccounted for, or even Charlie setting up a false dichotomy. \n\nSince there's way too much reasonable doubt, we shouldn't risk throwing out an innocent Goose this early. Let's all skip, buddy up, and keep a close eye on each other during the next round. If we stick together in groups of two or three, the Duck won't be able to make a move without being seen.\n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430751.286985, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Bob\u2019s timing is fair, but \u201clast person who saw Frank alive\u201d isn\u2019t the same as killer. I saw him alive in Electrical, then moved up into Medbay, and Bob saw me there right after. If I\u2019d killed and just walked into Bob for an alibi, that would be a really reckless route.\n\nThe part that still stands out to me is Eve being mostly unaccounted for after Weapons, and Alice being the reporter with the body in Electrical. I\u2019m not saying hard vote either of them, but those are the two routes we need more eyes on next round.\n\nI\u2019m okay with skipping here because the timing is too muddy, but please don\u2019t let the Duck use \u201cDiana saw him alive\u201d as an easy frame. Next round I\u2019m sticking with someone."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430823.5512216, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Yeah, I'm fully on board with skipping here. Bob laid out the timelines perfectly, and a wrong vote right now with only 5 of us left could be disastrous. \n\nEve is definitely the wild card since she has no one to vouch for her movements after Weapons, but Diana's timing is also tricky, and Alice could theoretically be pulling off a very tight self-report. There's just not enough concrete evidence to risk an ejection. Let's all skip, buddy up, and keep a very close eye on Eve and Diana next round. I'll stick with Alice if possible since we already share some trust.\n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430834.8359022, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I completely agree that skipping is the only safe play here. Since a few of you called me the wild card, I just want to defend my positioning: I went straight from Security to Weapons and was focused on my tasks there the entire time. If I had tried to sneak down to Electrical, I almost certainly would have crossed paths with Alice or Charlie in the Security/Weapons corridor area. \n\nI'm fine with being watched next round. Let's make sure we stick in groups of at least two or three so the Duck doesn't have an opportunity to isolate anyone. \n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430844.1078935, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I completely agree with the consensus. We've analyzed the timelines and there's simply too much reasonable doubt between Diana, Eve, and Alice. Throwing a vote right now with 5 of us left is too risky. Let's all just buddy up next round as discussed and keep our eyes peeled. I'm locking in my skip.\n\nskip"}}
